---
import {existsSync} from 'node:fs';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactBridge from '../components/ContactBridge.astro';
import {experience} from '../data/experience';
const hasHeadshot=existsSync('public/media/headshot.webp');
---
<Base title="About" description="Meet Toluwani Oluwole, a Dallas computer engineer completing a B.S. in Computer Engineering at Texas Tech, with experience at SureAttend and LuMATH." active="about">
  <section class="wrap page-intro about-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">About / Toluwani Oluwole</span><h1>I’m Tolu.<br/><span class="green-text">I follow the signal.</span></h1><p class="lead">From an API response to an amplifier pin, I like understanding why a system behaves the way it does.</p><p>I’m a computer engineer based in Dallas, Texas, completing my B.S. in Computer Engineering at Texas Tech University. My work spans full-stack products, AI infrastructure and embedded devices.</p></div>{hasHeadshot&&<figure class="portrait"><img src="/media/headshot.webp" width="240" height="300" alt="Portrait of Toluwani Oluwole" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Dallas, Texas</figcaption></figure>}</section>
  <section id="experience" class="section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">01 / Experience</span><h2>The work behind the work.</h2></div><div class="timeline">{experience.map(job=><article class:list={['timeline-row',{'compact-job':job.compact}]}><div class="eyebrow">{job.dates}</div><div><h3>{job.company}</h3><p class="job-role">{job.role}</p><p>{job.text}</p>{job.future&&<p class="future-title">{job.future}</p>}</div></article>)}</div></section>
  <section id="education" class="section wrap education"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Education</span><div><h2>Texas Tech University</h2><p class="lead">B.S. in Computer Engineering</p><dl><div><dt>Minors</dt><dd>Computer Science and Mathematics</dd></div><div><dt>Expected graduation</dt><dd>December 2026</dd></div><div><dt>GPA</dt><dd>3.6</dd></div></dl><p class="muted">Coursework includes Data Structures & Algorithms, Object-Oriented Programming, Software Engineering, Embedded Systems, Microcontrollers, Autonomous Driving and Cyber-Aerial Computing.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap approach"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">03 / How I work</span><h2>Start with the boundary.<br/>Test the assumption.</h2></div><div class="approach-grid"><article><span class="eyebrow">01 / Make contracts explicit</span><h3>Know what crosses the interface.</h3><p>At LuMATH, typed interfaces and backward-compatible migration planning made component responsibilities explicit. At SureAttend, that attention shows up in request validation and user-scoped APIs.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/recconnect/">See the application boundary ↗</a></article><article><span class="eyebrow">02 / Isolate the failure</span><h3>Follow the output, stage by stage.</h3><p>In the capstone, noise at the speaker led me through the signal chain to amplifier-enable sequencing. A working waveform was only one part of the system.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/sheet-music-to-sound-reader/">Read the debugging story ↗</a></article><article><span class="eyebrow">03 / Explain the reasoning</span><h3>Make the next person’s work clearer.</h3><p>Tutoring C/C++ and supporting engineering labs have made explanation part of my practice: identify the misunderstanding, inspect the behavior and make the next step concrete.</p><a class="text-link" href="/resume/">View my résumé ↗</a></article></div></section><ContactBridge/>
</Base>
